        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 5:25PM CDT by NWS Midland/Odessa TX</headline>
        <description>At 524 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10
miles east of Saragosa, or 28 miles southeast of Toyah, moving
northeast at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

This storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northwestern Pecos
and southeastern Reeves Counties.

This includes Interstate 10 between mile markers 220 and 227.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
